ed the the whole subplot  then you'll have these control panel  tools where you can change like the the  axes and the title and the um the color  of the plot window and things like that  oh and notice that all of the matplotlib  tools are readily available so  like the ones you know and love the zoom  and pan and home and all that are just  right there on the top  okay and then something i mentioned  before that we're really excited about  is this brand new scripting interface  which we just released with the the  latest release  um  and  so as well as this basic gui um  you can you can work with avoplot uh  from a scripting interface um and  although only a few commands are  currently um  implemented but we hope to to grow it  and also one thing we're hoping to to  achieve here is maybe get get more of  you developing on it as well which would  be fantastic  so it's basically designed to mimic  the pi plot interface um making it  really simple for people who already use  matplotlib to just like i said import  avo plot and plot and then it opens your  plot in in our program instead  um  and so that if you have existing scripts  for example they can already be changed  very easily  uh plugins which i think is is what  makes this really powerful um and very  very usable for people who maybe aren't  as avid as coders but maybe just  starting out  is uh is is the fact that it's a plug-in  interface  so the most simple the most simple  plug-in  like just a few lines of code um  will allow unsupported data files uh to  be loaded like  by a point and click of like file new  um but more complex ones allow you to  find define your own access specific  data series types  specific data processing tools you know  adding buttons and things like that  plugins are distributed using disk g  tills  and a bunch of so so loads of loads of  scripts like quick and dirty scripts are  written by scientists every day right  but we'd like to offer avo plot as sort  of a framework for them t